  "findings": [
    "Initial Settings entry and reopening show the full heading and eyebrow at960x600 and1280x720. Labels do not overlap.",
    "Back is partially below the scroll viewport initially; seven real Tab presses move focus to it and reveal its entire button. The intentional scroll hides the eyebrow; reopening restores the top.",
    "Loaded title, title return and actual world entry have readable actions and HUD; hero/reticle are not covered by peripheral HUD cards.",
    "Earlier controls/ability-sheet/pause/menu-scroll images show visible keyboard focus and readable content; the controls list and pause list are intentionally scrollable. The root/interface R1 receipts cover the broader remap, retained preference, cast, reset and modal-return paths.",
    "Settings/Help return to the title with Bow training focused, not the exact opener or primary Explore action. At960 the recorded Return briefly entered training before a real title return and mouse click entered Confluence. This known navigation-polish limitation is retained; no direct keyboard Explore-entry or opener-restoration claim."
  ],
